+Across this sequence, we have selected, guided, branched, connected, carved, sampled and copied. Each operation gives us something to build with and something more precise to question. What bodies are possible now? We can answer with a construction, try its limits, and carry the unresolved part into the next hall. In Soft Bodies, next, the record stays fixed while the positions move: a cube keeps every prescribed connection and still gives way. Ask what its support and collider must supply before believing the surface.
 
