+
+[^rhizome]: The rhizome is Gilles Deleuze and Félix Guattari’s figure, from *A Thousand Plateaus* (1980), defined against the tree: no root, any point joinable to any other. That opposition is why the opening here is a tree, and why the second policy is named for what a tree is not.
